WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.286 --> 00:00:01.725
- Some people will also
discourage you and say,

00:00:01.725 --> 00:00:03.206
"You know what, are you
sure you want to do this?

00:00:03.206 --> 00:00:04.558
"Are you sure, you want to wait?"

00:00:04.558 --> 00:00:05.717
Yeah, I'm not satisfied.

00:00:05.717 --> 00:00:06.787
I'm not fully satisfied,

00:00:06.787 --> 00:00:08.102
and I don't ever want to be.

00:00:08.102 --> 00:00:10.846
I don't want to regret
anything in life, ever.

00:00:10.846 --> 00:00:11.896
I do what I do.

00:00:11.896 --> 00:00:13.543
I do what I love.

00:00:13.543 --> 00:00:14.405
- Hello Believe Nation!

00:00:14.405 --> 00:00:15.623
My name is Evan Carmichael.

00:00:15.623 --> 00:00:16.951
My one word is believe,

00:00:16.951 --> 00:00:19.228
and I believe that
entrepreneurs will solve all

00:00:19.228 --> 00:00:21.212
of the world's major problems.

00:00:21.212 --> 00:00:22.538
So to help you on your journey today,

00:00:22.538 --> 00:00:23.371
we're going to learn

00:00:23.371 --> 00:00:25.538
from actress and
entrepreneur Deepika Padukone

00:00:25.538 --> 00:00:28.849
and my take on her top
ten rules to success.

00:00:28.849 --> 00:00:30.497
Rule number one is my personal favorite,

00:00:30.497 --> 00:00:31.330
and I'd love to know

00:00:31.330 --> 00:00:32.872
which one you guys like the best.

00:00:32.872 --> 00:00:34.484
And as always, as you're watching,

00:00:34.484 --> 00:00:35.978
if you hear something
that really resonates

00:00:35.978 --> 00:00:38.225
with you, please leave
it in the comments below.

00:00:38.225 --> 00:00:39.107
Put quotes around it,

00:00:39.107 --> 00:00:40.453
so other people can be inspired.

00:00:40.453 --> 00:00:42.190
Might win a prize as well.

00:00:42.190 --> 00:00:43.772
And also, when you write it down,

00:00:43.772 --> 00:00:44.988
it's much more likely to stick

00:00:44.988 --> 00:00:46.732
for yourself, as well.

00:00:46.732 --> 00:00:47.565
Enjoy.

00:00:47.565 --> 00:00:48.891
(swish sound)

00:00:48.891 --> 00:00:50.613
(basketball bounce)

00:00:50.613 --> 00:00:53.446
(uplifting music)

00:01:00.579 --> 00:01:03.478
(stamp slamming)
Believe, you know?

00:01:03.478 --> 00:01:05.725
Things will always not go your way.

00:01:05.725 --> 00:01:06.639
There will be times

00:01:06.639 --> 00:01:08.912
where things will be difficult.

00:01:08.912 --> 00:01:10.527
There will be times when you wanted things

00:01:10.527 --> 00:01:11.610
to be a certain way,

00:01:11.610 --> 00:01:13.693
and they don't go that way.

00:01:13.693 --> 00:01:15.086
But I think, through the years,

00:01:15.086 --> 00:01:16.260
I think the one thing that I've learned

00:01:16.260 --> 00:01:19.038
is to be patient and to really believe

00:01:19.038 --> 00:01:19.917
in yourself.

00:01:19.917 --> 00:01:22.117
I mean you can have,
you know, amazing people

00:01:22.117 --> 00:01:24.571
around you telling you different things.

00:01:24.571 --> 00:01:26.314
Some people really believe in your vision,

00:01:26.314 --> 00:01:27.340
and some people won't.

00:01:27.340 --> 00:01:28.519
Some people will also discourage you,

00:01:28.519 --> 00:01:29.352
and say, "You know what,

00:01:29.352 --> 00:01:30.364
"are you sure you want to do this?

00:01:30.364 --> 00:01:31.509
"Are you sure, you want to wait?

00:01:31.509 --> 00:01:32.342
"Are you...

00:01:32.342 --> 00:01:33.715
"You know, why don't
you try something else

00:01:33.715 --> 00:01:35.085
"or do something else?"

00:01:35.085 --> 00:01:37.100
I think it's important to be...

00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:39.108
I mean, at least, I fortunately had a lot

00:01:39.108 --> 00:01:40.853
of clarity about what I wanted to do

00:01:40.853 --> 00:01:42.410
with my life and for myself,

00:01:42.410 --> 00:01:43.243
and,

00:01:45.106 --> 00:01:46.691
you know,

00:01:46.691 --> 00:01:48.932
I've been very patient through all of it.

00:01:48.932 --> 00:01:49.765
And I'm not someone--

00:01:49.765 --> 00:01:51.651
I don't give up easily.

00:01:51.651 --> 00:01:53.306
- You just keep the faith.

00:01:53.306 --> 00:01:55.268
- Yeah, I keep the faith.

00:01:55.268 --> 00:01:56.101
I'd never give up.

00:01:56.101 --> 00:02:00.147
The minute you tell me
that I can't do something,

00:02:00.147 --> 00:02:03.558
I work that much harder to prove,

00:02:03.558 --> 00:02:05.873
not to people, but to myself

00:02:05.873 --> 00:02:07.136
that I can do it.

00:02:07.136 --> 00:02:08.521
It can be anything.

00:02:08.521 --> 00:02:09.478
(swoosh sound)
So every film

00:02:09.478 --> 00:02:11.395
has its own challenges.

00:02:13.011 --> 00:02:15.921
But overall, I think there is a perception

00:02:15.921 --> 00:02:18.560
that the film industry is all glamorous,

00:02:18.560 --> 00:02:20.727
and it's easy, and it's...

00:02:22.743 --> 00:02:24.152
I think a lot of people feel like people

00:02:24.152 --> 00:02:26.851
in the industry are very privileged,

00:02:26.851 --> 00:02:28.528
but that's not true.

00:02:28.528 --> 00:02:30.983
There's a lot of hard work and commitment

00:02:30.983 --> 00:02:33.576
and dedication and sacrifices that go

00:02:33.576 --> 00:02:37.865
into being who we are
or achieving what we do.

00:02:37.865 --> 00:02:40.103
It's very easy to buy your ticket and sit

00:02:40.103 --> 00:02:41.351
in a theater and watch a movie

00:02:41.351 --> 00:02:42.418
for two and a half hours,

00:02:42.418 --> 00:02:43.720
and be entertained or not

00:02:43.720 --> 00:02:45.438
and that's totally fair,

00:02:45.438 --> 00:02:47.346
but there's a lot of hard work that goes

00:02:47.346 --> 00:02:48.928
into making that possible,

00:02:48.928 --> 00:02:51.016
which I think only people who are related

00:02:51.016 --> 00:02:52.023
in the film industry

00:02:52.023 --> 00:02:55.936
in some way will know
the full extent of that.

00:02:55.936 --> 00:02:58.271
(swoosh sound)
I'm extremely ambitious.

00:02:58.271 --> 00:02:59.810
I know exactly what I want,

00:02:59.810 --> 00:03:01.125
what I want to achieve for myself,

00:03:01.125 --> 00:03:02.324
the kind of films I want to do,

00:03:02.324 --> 00:03:04.820
the kind of people that
I want to work with,

00:03:04.820 --> 00:03:07.166
and that will always
be an ongoing process.

00:03:07.166 --> 00:03:08.066
Since childhood,

00:03:08.066 --> 00:03:09.677
I've always known what I wanted to do.

00:03:09.677 --> 00:03:12.900
Today, I'm living that dream,

00:03:12.900 --> 00:03:14.016
but I always say,

00:03:14.016 --> 00:03:15.087
I'm not satisfied.

00:03:15.087 --> 00:03:16.240
I'm not fully satisfied,

00:03:16.240 --> 00:03:17.981
and I don't ever want to be.

00:03:17.981 --> 00:03:18.887
I want that hunger.

00:03:18.887 --> 00:03:21.046
I want that motivation to keep me going.

00:03:21.046 --> 00:03:21.879
- It's the hunger

00:03:21.879 --> 00:03:22.957
that keeps you going.
- Yeah.

00:03:22.957 --> 00:03:24.014
(swoosh sound)
Do I appreciate

00:03:24.014 --> 00:03:26.910
and admire a lot of actresses around me

00:03:26.910 --> 00:03:29.553
and people who've been around me before?

00:03:29.553 --> 00:03:30.803
Of course I do.

00:03:31.762 --> 00:03:32.959
In few films that they've done,

00:03:32.959 --> 00:03:34.746
or in the performances that they've given,

00:03:34.746 --> 00:03:38.359
or in the way that they've
conducted themselves,

00:03:38.359 --> 00:03:40.176
of course I admire them,

00:03:40.176 --> 00:03:41.831
but I do not want my career

00:03:41.831 --> 00:03:45.096
to be like anyone else's but my own.

00:03:45.096 --> 00:03:47.912
Because it's a very very personal thing,

00:03:47.912 --> 00:03:48.919
and something that I like,

00:03:48.919 --> 00:03:50.375
somebody else may not like,

00:03:50.375 --> 00:03:51.995
so it cannot be.

00:03:51.995 --> 00:03:53.025
Even if I want it to be,

00:03:53.025 --> 00:03:54.108
it cannot be.

00:03:55.048 --> 00:03:57.661
And I want to be remembered

00:03:57.661 --> 00:04:01.381
for my own individual sense of everything.

00:04:01.381 --> 00:04:02.485
Whether it's style,

00:04:02.485 --> 00:04:03.507
whether it's films,

00:04:03.507 --> 00:04:04.906
whether it's career graph,

00:04:04.906 --> 00:04:05.906
whether it's

00:04:07.412 --> 00:04:09.498
values that you stick by.

00:04:09.498 --> 00:04:10.666
It has to be your own.

00:04:10.666 --> 00:04:12.266
(swoosh sound)
- Tendency to be cynical

00:04:12.266 --> 00:04:13.972
when actors go outside

00:04:13.972 --> 00:04:15.530
of their country and work.

00:04:15.530 --> 00:04:17.595
We've seen that happen
with actors in the past.

00:04:17.595 --> 00:04:18.795
There's, you know, some people say,

00:04:18.795 --> 00:04:20.319
"What's the big deal?"

00:04:20.319 --> 00:04:21.152
How do you view it?

00:04:21.152 --> 00:04:22.109
I mean, I know for you,

00:04:22.109 --> 00:04:23.688
you've been staying around longer.

00:04:23.688 --> 00:04:25.451
It's not like you're moving to the West.

00:04:25.451 --> 00:04:27.725
It's not like you're
ditching Hindi movies,

00:04:27.725 --> 00:04:29.852
and you're going to
completely move to the West

00:04:29.852 --> 00:04:31.210
and become an American actor.

00:04:31.210 --> 00:04:34.602
Do you see this as just another exciting

00:04:34.602 --> 00:04:36.232
kind of stop in the journey?

00:04:36.232 --> 00:04:40.404
Yeah, I think you want
to keep adding layers

00:04:40.404 --> 00:04:41.893
to yourself,

00:04:41.893 --> 00:04:43.083
to your life,

00:04:43.083 --> 00:04:44.505
to your career,

00:04:44.505 --> 00:04:46.941
I don't view them as two
separate careers anyway.

00:04:46.941 --> 00:04:50.627
I think that's the biggest
mistake people make.

00:04:50.627 --> 00:04:53.665
I look at it as one long journey

00:04:53.665 --> 00:04:54.681
with different things

00:04:54.681 --> 00:04:55.981
that could be thrown at you,

00:04:55.981 --> 00:04:57.043
different challenges.

00:04:57.043 --> 00:05:00.297
And how do you make them your own?

00:05:00.297 --> 00:05:01.990
And, you know, I see

00:05:01.990 --> 00:05:03.427
that people from China,

00:05:03.427 --> 00:05:04.779
people from Australia,

00:05:04.779 --> 00:05:06.306
people from England,

00:05:06.306 --> 00:05:08.710
everyone's done it so successfully.

00:05:08.710 --> 00:05:09.543
I mean, of course,

00:05:09.543 --> 00:05:11.904
everyone's choices are individual,

00:05:11.904 --> 00:05:13.815
and, you know, I'm sure

00:05:13.815 --> 00:05:15.857
different actors have different ways

00:05:15.857 --> 00:05:18.649
of how they want to maneuver their career

00:05:18.649 --> 00:05:20.624
and what they want to do with their lives

00:05:20.624 --> 00:05:22.160
and with their careers,

00:05:22.160 --> 00:05:24.415
and it's also a huge time
commitment, you know?

00:05:24.415 --> 00:05:26.120
It's not just about being in the movie.

00:05:26.120 --> 00:05:26.953
It's also...

00:05:26.953 --> 00:05:28.870
It's a huge commitment.

00:05:30.564 --> 00:05:32.710
But I was willing to go through that.

00:05:32.710 --> 00:05:35.329
You know, I was willing
to make that commitment.

00:05:35.329 --> 00:05:36.662
I was willing to

00:05:37.641 --> 00:05:38.809
tread this path

00:05:38.809 --> 00:05:40.758
and experience this journey.

00:05:40.758 --> 00:05:44.508
I don't want to regret
anything in life ever.

00:05:45.436 --> 00:05:47.596
Eight years, ten years, 15 years, 20 years

00:05:47.596 --> 00:05:48.885
down the line.
- And say that the

00:05:48.885 --> 00:05:49.809
opportunity came,

00:05:49.809 --> 00:05:50.883
but I didn't...
- The opportunity came

00:05:50.883 --> 00:05:52.901
and "Ugh! I wish I did!"

00:05:52.901 --> 00:05:54.289
You know, at least now I know I did,

00:05:54.289 --> 00:05:56.013
and if it works, great,

00:05:56.013 --> 00:05:58.460
if not, you know, at least I know I tried.

00:05:58.460 --> 00:06:00.681
(swoosh sound)
- What does power mean to you?

00:06:00.681 --> 00:06:04.630
And what freedom does
this power afford you?

00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:06.052
- Nothing.

00:06:06.052 --> 00:06:06.940
Nothing.

00:06:06.940 --> 00:06:08.857
It means nothing to me.

00:06:11.706 --> 00:06:12.832
I do what I do.

00:06:12.832 --> 00:06:14.315
I do what I love.

00:06:14.315 --> 00:06:17.311
The money happens to come.

00:06:17.311 --> 00:06:18.764
It means nothing, you know?

00:06:18.764 --> 00:06:20.510
And I know so many people

00:06:20.510 --> 00:06:22.822
and my own experiences here.

00:06:22.822 --> 00:06:24.709
You can have everything in the world,

00:06:24.709 --> 00:06:27.470
but if you're not happy,

00:06:27.470 --> 00:06:28.531
you can do nothing with it.

00:06:28.531 --> 00:06:29.787
And it really means nothing.

00:06:29.787 --> 00:06:31.575
So for me, if it's there, it's there.

00:06:31.575 --> 00:06:34.802
If it's not there, it's not there.

00:06:34.802 --> 00:06:35.731
It doesn't matter.

00:06:35.731 --> 00:06:38.731
For me, quality time with my family,

00:06:39.962 --> 00:06:41.623
going on family vacations,

00:06:41.623 --> 00:06:43.400
spending quality time with them at home,

00:06:43.400 --> 00:06:45.368
cooking a meal in my kitchen,

00:06:45.368 --> 00:06:48.160
spending time with my friends,

00:06:48.160 --> 00:06:51.991
being creatively satisfied with a film

00:06:51.991 --> 00:06:53.934
or with a part,

00:06:53.934 --> 00:06:56.949
being challenged in that sense,

00:06:56.949 --> 00:06:59.321
going up on stage
receiving a Filmfare Award.

00:06:59.321 --> 00:07:01.743
These are the things that
I really really value.

00:07:01.743 --> 00:07:04.761
This makes absolutely no difference.

00:07:04.761 --> 00:07:05.739
(swoosh sound)
- You know, sacrifices,

00:07:05.739 --> 00:07:07.730
social sacrifices,

00:07:07.730 --> 00:07:08.894
sacrificing I think for me,

00:07:08.894 --> 00:07:10.418
my biggest sacrifice has been the fact

00:07:10.418 --> 00:07:11.956
that I don't live with my family.

00:07:11.956 --> 00:07:14.058
I've had to move away,

00:07:14.058 --> 00:07:14.969
so of course there are days

00:07:14.969 --> 00:07:17.529
when, you know, I go home.

00:07:17.529 --> 00:07:18.362
I miss them.

00:07:18.362 --> 00:07:20.843
I miss the fact that over a meal,

00:07:20.843 --> 00:07:22.483
I don't have my parents or my sister

00:07:22.483 --> 00:07:24.783
to talk to, you know?

00:07:24.783 --> 00:07:27.047
Just talk about what my day was like,

00:07:27.047 --> 00:07:28.685
or of course I can do it on the phone,

00:07:28.685 --> 00:07:30.647
but it's different when, you know?

00:07:30.647 --> 00:07:32.314
Your face to say it.

00:07:34.632 --> 00:07:36.744
So there are certain
sacrifices that one has

00:07:36.744 --> 00:07:38.197
to make, diet-wise, you know?

00:07:38.197 --> 00:07:39.422
I enjoy eating.

00:07:39.422 --> 00:07:40.478
I love eating.

00:07:40.478 --> 00:07:42.960
Thankfully, I'm not someone who puts

00:07:42.960 --> 00:07:45.695
on weight easily, but I have a weakness

00:07:45.695 --> 00:07:47.313
for sweets and chocolates,

00:07:47.313 --> 00:07:49.563
and I have to control that.

00:07:50.500 --> 00:07:52.664
So yeah, it comes with its...

00:07:52.664 --> 00:07:55.509
Or in the way that I
conduct myself, you know?

00:07:55.509 --> 00:07:57.451
I think that is also a sacrifice.

00:07:57.451 --> 00:07:59.566
If sometimes there's a certain way

00:07:59.566 --> 00:08:00.399
I'd like to be,

00:08:00.399 --> 00:08:01.685
I also have to realize that I have

00:08:01.685 --> 00:08:03.530
to be socially responsible.

00:08:03.530 --> 00:08:04.905
(swoosh sound)
You know,

00:08:04.905 --> 00:08:06.897
as actors and as artists,

00:08:06.897 --> 00:08:10.218
you're constantly looking for challenges,

00:08:10.218 --> 00:08:11.819
either in the kind of role that you do

00:08:11.819 --> 00:08:13.819
or in the kind of movie,

00:08:16.209 --> 00:08:17.546
or like even when I did Cocktail.

00:08:17.546 --> 00:08:19.302
Like, Cocktail was completely out

00:08:19.302 --> 00:08:20.591
of my comfort zone,

00:08:20.591 --> 00:08:23.478
and I think this was
the right film for me.

00:08:23.478 --> 00:08:25.561
I remember being offered,

00:08:26.740 --> 00:08:27.884
you know it's public knowledge.

00:08:27.884 --> 00:08:29.065
Everyone knows.
- Yeah, yeah, Furious 7.

00:08:29.065 --> 00:08:30.212
- I was offered Furious 7,

00:08:30.212 --> 00:08:33.300
and we tried so hard to make that work,

00:08:33.300 --> 00:08:34.740
and it didn't.

00:08:34.740 --> 00:08:37.072
And today, when I look back, you know,

00:08:37.072 --> 00:08:41.155
a part of me is like, it
just wasn't meant to be.

00:08:43.376 --> 00:08:44.351
So, I always feel like

00:08:44.351 --> 00:08:47.081
there's always a right
time for everything,

00:08:47.081 --> 00:08:48.782
and I think that this, kind of...

00:08:48.782 --> 00:08:51.688
this was just the right
time for it to happen.

00:08:51.688 --> 00:08:54.208
And it was the right kind of challenge,

00:08:54.208 --> 00:08:55.644
and in a right way,

00:08:55.644 --> 00:08:58.274
I mean of course the character's exciting,

00:08:58.274 --> 00:08:59.595
but I've never done this kind of--

00:08:59.595 --> 00:09:01.090
I've done an action film before

00:09:01.090 --> 00:09:03.275
but I've not done this
kind of action before.

00:09:03.275 --> 00:09:05.579
I really don't know what
success means to me,

00:09:05.579 --> 00:09:06.949
but I think for me,

00:09:06.949 --> 00:09:09.365
to be truly successful is to be at peace

00:09:09.365 --> 00:09:13.097
with myself and to be
happy with every day.

00:09:13.097 --> 00:09:16.188
I think depression has taught me

00:09:16.188 --> 00:09:18.749
how fragile my life is

00:09:18.749 --> 00:09:20.525
or how fragile our lives are.

00:09:20.525 --> 00:09:24.025
And it's made me value people and emotions

00:09:24.945 --> 00:09:26.028
and feelings.

00:09:27.270 --> 00:09:29.360
So for me, it's not the material things.

00:09:29.360 --> 00:09:32.460
It's not the numbers, it's not--

00:09:32.460 --> 00:09:34.156
Because there's always more.

00:09:34.156 --> 00:09:35.061
You can be number one,

00:09:35.061 --> 00:09:36.007
and then you will still want

00:09:36.007 --> 00:09:37.127
to keep going at that.

00:09:37.127 --> 00:09:39.196
Or, you know, you can be...

00:09:39.196 --> 00:09:41.029
You know, you can have X amount of money,

00:09:41.029 --> 00:09:42.341
and there's no end to that.

00:09:42.341 --> 00:09:44.442
So as far as material
things are concerned,

00:09:44.442 --> 00:09:45.803
I think there's no end to it.

00:09:45.803 --> 00:09:46.907
You'll just, you know,

00:09:46.907 --> 00:09:48.490
people want more and more and more,

00:09:48.490 --> 00:09:50.160
and that's human nature,

00:09:50.160 --> 00:09:52.152
but to be truly at peace with yourself,

00:09:52.152 --> 00:09:53.152
and to be...

00:09:55.671 --> 00:09:57.700
That's is success for me.

00:09:57.700 --> 00:09:58.851
(swoosh sound)
- About a year ago,

00:09:58.851 --> 00:10:01.695
I get a call from Paramount saying,

00:10:01.695 --> 00:10:03.431
you know, they're casting for this film,

00:10:03.431 --> 00:10:05.576
and I flew down and I met D.J.,

00:10:05.576 --> 00:10:06.999
my director Caruso,

00:10:06.999 --> 00:10:09.042
and then Vin found out in LA

00:10:09.042 --> 00:10:10.238
that I was in Toronto,

00:10:10.238 --> 00:10:12.273
and so overnight, luckily, I had a visa,

00:10:12.273 --> 00:10:13.106
and he said,

00:10:13.106 --> 00:10:14.624
"I want her to come and see me."

00:10:14.624 --> 00:10:17.083
So overnight, I flew down from Toronto

00:10:17.083 --> 00:10:19.874
to Los Angeles to see Vin,

00:10:19.874 --> 00:10:22.323
and suddenly, in the middle of the night,

00:10:22.323 --> 00:10:25.148
we're doing this 45-minute photoshoot.

00:10:25.148 --> 00:10:27.084
Professional, with
lights and this and that,

00:10:27.084 --> 00:10:28.510
and I was like, what is going on?

00:10:28.510 --> 00:10:31.912
Because I didn't know if I got the part.

00:10:31.912 --> 00:10:35.014
I still don't know if I got the part.

00:10:35.014 --> 00:10:35.847
He just...

00:10:35.847 --> 00:10:39.318
We just got into this
really serious photo shoot.

00:10:39.318 --> 00:10:42.308
I don't know if you guys
have seen the picture,

00:10:42.308 --> 00:10:43.519
and that was it.

00:10:43.519 --> 00:10:44.637
- That picture right there?

00:10:44.637 --> 00:10:45.589
- That's the one!

00:10:45.589 --> 00:10:46.908
In his house, yeah.

00:10:46.908 --> 00:10:47.741
- Yes.
- That's the one,

00:10:47.741 --> 00:10:48.574
and he just put it up.

00:10:48.574 --> 00:10:49.608
I said, "I do hope you know

00:10:49.608 --> 00:10:50.740
"that if you put that picture up,

00:10:50.740 --> 00:10:53.014
"it means I'm doing this movie."

00:10:53.014 --> 00:10:54.655
He still didn't say anything.

00:10:54.655 --> 00:10:56.252
(audience laughing)
He just put it up.

00:10:56.252 --> 00:10:57.173
- And so, when that went up,

00:10:57.173 --> 00:10:58.239
you got all these calls

00:10:58.239 --> 00:10:59.616
from your fans and friends

00:10:59.616 --> 00:11:01.090
congratulating you, right?
- Yes,

00:11:01.090 --> 00:11:02.533
and I didn't know what to say to them,

00:11:02.533 --> 00:11:04.373
because I had journalists
calling me from India

00:11:04.373 --> 00:11:05.993
and saying, "Oh my god,
you're doing this movie?"

00:11:05.993 --> 00:11:08.830
And I didn't know what to say.

00:11:08.830 --> 00:11:10.263
I just, I was like,

00:11:10.263 --> 00:11:11.644
"I don't even know if that's Vin.

00:11:11.644 --> 00:11:13.044
"I don't know what you
guys are talking about."

00:11:13.044 --> 00:11:14.531
(audience laughing)

00:11:14.531 --> 00:11:16.309
- But I mean, or their
looking at it going,

00:11:16.309 --> 00:11:17.621
"There's a romance going on."

00:11:17.621 --> 00:11:19.213
That's what you would
get from that as well,

00:11:19.213 --> 00:11:20.046
which there--

00:11:20.046 --> 00:11:21.084
Oh, look at that face.

00:11:21.084 --> 00:11:22.271
(audience laughing)

00:11:22.271 --> 00:11:23.463
Does that mean there is?

00:11:23.463 --> 00:11:26.003
Because that's what the rumor is.

00:11:26.003 --> 00:11:30.003
- Well, there's no smoke
without fire, you know.

00:11:31.222 --> 00:11:33.124
Look at that.

00:11:33.124 --> 00:11:34.129
- So?
- But...

00:11:34.129 --> 00:11:37.844
(audience laughing)

00:11:37.844 --> 00:11:39.844
But it's all in my head!

00:11:41.078 --> 00:11:41.911
You know?

00:11:41.911 --> 00:11:43.504
- It's in his head right there.

00:11:43.504 --> 00:11:46.884
(audience laughing)

00:11:46.884 --> 00:11:48.166
Puttin' stuff in his head right there.

00:11:48.166 --> 00:11:49.159
- (laughing)

00:11:49.159 --> 00:11:51.285
So yeah, I mean in my head, I think, like,

00:11:51.285 --> 00:11:52.736
yeah like we're together,

00:11:52.736 --> 00:11:54.486
and we have this amazing chemistry

00:11:54.486 --> 00:11:55.975
and we live together,

00:11:55.975 --> 00:11:58.035
and we have these amazing babies,

00:11:58.035 --> 00:12:00.035
but it's all in my head.

00:12:00.897 --> 00:12:01.839
- Now you just became crazy.

00:12:01.839 --> 00:12:04.272
I don't know what happened.

00:12:04.272 --> 00:12:05.303
At first, it was a crush,

00:12:05.303 --> 00:12:06.161
and now you have babies.

00:12:06.161 --> 00:12:07.741
I don't know.

00:12:07.741 --> 00:12:09.074
- Never a crush.

00:12:11.769 --> 00:12:13.127
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:12:13.127 --> 00:12:16.504
I made this video because
Meera Patel asked me to.

00:12:16.504 --> 00:12:17.607
So if there's a famous entrepreneur

00:12:17.607 --> 00:12:19.118
that you want me to profile next,

00:12:19.118 --> 00:12:20.360
check out the link in the description

00:12:20.360 --> 00:12:22.648
and you can go and cast your vote.

00:12:22.648 --> 00:12:24.399
I'd also love to know which clip resonated

00:12:24.399 --> 00:12:25.237
the most with you.

00:12:25.237 --> 00:12:27.047
What lesson are you going
to take from this video

00:12:27.047 --> 00:12:28.991
and immediately apply to your life

00:12:28.991 --> 00:12:30.495
or to your business somehow?

00:12:30.495 --> 00:12:31.965
Leave it down in the comments below.

00:12:31.965 --> 00:12:32.920
I'm really curious to find out

00:12:32.920 --> 00:12:34.217
what you have to say.

00:12:34.217 --> 00:12:36.119
I also want to give a
quick shout out to Lauren.

00:12:36.119 --> 00:12:37.935
Lauren, thank you so much
for picking up a copy

00:12:37.935 --> 00:12:38.768
of my book Your One Word

00:12:38.768 --> 00:12:41.343
and making that video
on your YouTube channel.

00:12:41.343 --> 00:12:43.383
I really really really
appreciate your support,

00:12:43.383 --> 00:12:45.966
and I'm so glad that you enjoyed my book.

00:12:45.966 --> 00:12:47.632
- This week, I read Your One Word

00:12:47.632 --> 00:12:49.000
by Evan Carmichael.

00:12:49.000 --> 00:12:50.517
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:12:50.517 --> 00:12:51.887
I believe in you.

00:12:51.887 --> 00:12:53.808
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:12:53.808 --> 00:12:56.071
and whatever your one word is.

00:12:56.071 --> 00:12:57.205
Much love.

00:12:57.205 --> 00:12:58.493
I'll see you soon.

00:12:58.493 --> 00:12:59.799
(swoosh sound)

00:12:59.799 --> 00:13:02.799
(basketball bounce)

00:13:04.618 --> 00:13:07.201
- Everyday, every individual is

00:13:09.447 --> 00:13:11.663
fighting a different battle.

00:13:11.663 --> 00:13:12.496
We may not--

00:13:12.496 --> 00:13:13.711
we all come to our work place.

00:13:13.711 --> 00:13:15.749
We all meet each other
for eight, ten hours,

00:13:15.749 --> 00:13:17.525
and we all laugh and joke

00:13:17.525 --> 00:13:19.355
and move on with our lives,

00:13:19.355 --> 00:13:22.429
but each one of us is carrying something.

00:13:22.429 --> 00:13:23.790
You know, and it's important for us

00:13:23.790 --> 00:13:25.094
to remember that.

00:13:25.094 --> 00:13:26.830
We're all flawed in our different ways,

00:13:26.830 --> 00:13:29.293
but I think it's important
for us to identify.

00:13:29.293 --> 00:13:30.988
Like, for me, I've identified

00:13:30.988 --> 00:13:32.079
what my strengths are,

00:13:32.079 --> 00:13:33.174
what my weaknesses are,

00:13:33.174 --> 00:13:34.459
and I've come to terms with that,

00:13:34.459 --> 00:13:36.845
and that has made me a happy person today.

00:13:36.845 --> 00:13:39.579
We should do what makes us happy,

00:13:39.579 --> 00:13:40.714
what drives us.

00:13:40.714 --> 00:13:41.569
If you're going to do something

00:13:41.569 --> 00:13:42.858
that you're not interested in doing,

00:13:42.858 --> 00:13:43.930
your heart's not there,

00:13:43.930 --> 00:13:44.763
so I think it's very important

00:13:44.763 --> 00:13:46.513
to follow your heart.

00:13:46.513 --> 00:13:49.026
Every decision that I make,

00:13:49.026 --> 00:13:51.932
and not just relationship-wise,

00:13:51.932 --> 00:13:53.846
everything that I do,

00:13:53.846 --> 00:13:57.929
including the films that
I choose to be a part of

00:13:59.908 --> 00:14:01.789
come straight from the heart.

00:14:01.789 --> 00:14:02.622
So, I think sometimes

00:14:02.622 --> 00:14:04.495
people might question my choice of films,

00:14:04.495 --> 00:14:07.549
people might question
various other things,

00:14:07.549 --> 00:14:09.070
but I think at that point,

00:14:09.070 --> 00:14:11.289
I'm just thinking from the heart.

00:14:11.289 --> 00:14:12.122
(swoosh sound)

